WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.600
After breaking into worldwide superstardom
with Lethal Weapon 4, Jet Li became one of

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.440
cinema's most renowned martial arts stars.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.500
From sham marriages to global disasters to
the rumors around his health, here's the untold

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.980
truth of Jet Li.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:23.000
In 1973, the legendary actor and director
Bruce Lee passed away under mysterious circumstances,

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.340
leaving China, America, and the rest of the
movie-loving world in shock.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.759
The following year, the 11-year old Jet Li
was performing a kung fu demonstration in

00:00:31.759 --> 00:00:36.350
Hong Kong when he was approached by a movie
producer and asked how he felt about becoming

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.820
the next Bruce Lee.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.020
Speaking to TalkAsia in 2003, Li recalled
the encounter.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:42.820
He said:

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:46.840
"When [the] movie studio producer [talked]
to me, [he said] 'Hi, little kid, when you

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.270
grow up, [do] you want to become [an] action
star?

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.180
I [said], 'Okay, why not!'

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.920
So since then, every year the producer came
to me to look at me.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.989
[He would say], 'Okay, you are still a little
boy, [you] can't make [movies].

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:00.520
I want to wait [for] you.'"

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:05.100
Although he had greatly admired Bruce Lee,
as a young boy Jet Li couldn't imagine that

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:09.320
his name would ever be mentioned in the same
breath as the martial arts star.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.300
Li added:

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:15.160
"I remember I found him very talented, a very
talented actor and martial artist.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.460
But I [didn't] know how to make [movies] [...] I
was just 11."

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.900
Jet Li had turned 17 by the time the producer
decided he was ready to make his debut feature

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:24.700
film.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.400
He was cast in Shaolin Temple, the first in
a series of movies that established him as

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.840
a star in China.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:35.400
1974 turned out to be quite the eventful year
for Li.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.460
Not only did the 11-year-old find him catching
the interest of Chinese movie studios, but

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:43.780
he also got to perform in front of the U.S.
president.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.049
Li and the Chinese national Wushu team were
invited to the White House, where they put

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:50.630
on a show for Richard Nixon.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:55.180
Nixon wasn't exactly popular at the time,
and after he saw what Li could do, he apparently

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.400
offered him the job of protecting him.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:02.020
According to We Are The Mighty, the president
jokingly asked if Li would consider becoming

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.980
his personal muscle once he was old enough
to work.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.680
Li's reply is said to have left those in attendance
stunned.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.340
He allegedly insisted:

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.940
"No, I don't want to protect any individual.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:17.200
When I grow up, I want to defend my one billion
Chinese countrymen!"

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.120
The silence that fell over the room was broken
by then-Secretary of State, Henry Kissinger,

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.020
who quipped:

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:27.160
"Heavens, such a young boy and he already
speaks like a diplomat."

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:33.000
During his candid 2003 interview with TalkAsia,
Li was asked if there was any truth to the

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.880
rumors that his hotel room had been bugged
during his first visit to the United States.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.020
The Nixon administration were found to have
frequently spied on their political rivals

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:46.590
using hidden mics, and the Chinese government
were apparently very wary about sending the

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.680
Wushu team on a tour of America, knowing that
they could potentially be targeted for information.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.900
They were so wary, in fact, that they warned
the traveling team members to be careful about

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:00.840
what they said at all times, including when
they were in the privacy of their hotel rooms.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.060
During his interview, Li confirmed:

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:03.880
"It's true.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:08.320
At that time, China and America [had] just
started [a] relationship between the two countries.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.640
It is so funny!

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:13.380
When I went there I wanted to try [to see
if] they have a bug or not.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.820
So in New York, [in] a big hotel, I talked
to the mirrors."

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:21.640
Li claims that he said out loud that he would
really like some chocolate and ice cream.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:27.420
To his surprise, the treats he had wished
for in his private quarters miraculously materialized.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.580
"I opened the door, anything I asked on the
table.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.780
I thought ‘wow, it’s true’, it's fun!"

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:42.320
Li's first appearance in a Hollywood movie
was as the villain in 1998's Lethal Weapon

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:45.130
4, but he wasn't used to playing a bad guy
at the time.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:50.200
He got his chance to play the hero in western
cinema two years later when he was cast as

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.020
the male lead in 2000's Romeo Must Die, starring
opposite Aaliyah.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:00.520
Like Li, the R&amp;B singer-turned-actress was
trying to earn her stripes in Tinseltown.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.520
Sadly, she died before she really got the
chance to establish herself.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:10.880
On August 25th 2001, the 22-year-old boarded
a small plane headed to Miami, but the aircraft

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:15.600
would never reach its destination, having
been dangerously overloaded before take-off.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.260
Aaliyah, as well as her staffers and the crew
of the aircraft, were all killed.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.700
When Li later returned to Vancouver, where
Romeo Must Die had been filmed, he found it

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.230
difficult to be back there.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.560
He told IGN:

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:32.640
"I have some memories of this very beautiful
city but it still makes me think about Aaliyah.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.880
We worked together here for a few months.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.620
She was such a talented girl and some locations
when you pass by every day, you still think

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:40.620
about her."

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:46.360
Romeo Must Die didn't exactly blow the critics
away, but Li was considered one of the movie's

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.200
highlights.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.060
The box office numbers were a little more
convincing, however.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:56.560
The film managed to rake in $91 million worldwide
from a budget of $25 million, which was seen

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.720
as a pretty decent haul at the time.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.800
All things considered it was a success for
Li, who felt so comfortable with his future

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:07.060
prospects that he went on to turn down a role
in the Matrix sequels.

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:11.520
Speaking to TalkAsia, the star explained that
he had to make a choice between The Matrix

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:17.260
sequel, for which he was reportedly offered
the part of Seraph, and Zhang Yimou's Hero.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.400
Li mused:

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:22.160
"Sometimes you get something and sometimes
you lose something."

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:26.720
Li claimed to be a fan of the Wachowskis,
but added that he wasn't a fan of what the

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.160
sibling directors did to the action genre.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:30.200
Li explained:

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.900
"After The Matrix, everybody [did] action
[movies] with people fighting while flying

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.780
around.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.660
Suddenly everyone can fight.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.980
Man can [fight], girl can [fight], little
boy can [fight], even [cartoons] can do the

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:41.780
same thing.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.780
In this movie, everyone really can [fight]."

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:49.680
His decision to favor Hero over The Matrix
sequels paid off, however, as the Chinese

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.520
wuxia film won widespread approval — while
The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix Revolutions

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.380
fizzed out with critics.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:58.760
“Woah.”

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.580
After his breakthrough in America, Li found
himself spending more and more time in the

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.620
United States.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:10.220
He decided that it made sense to apply for
American citizenship, which he was duly granted.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:16.580
But he renounced both his American and Chinese
citizenship in 2009 in order to move to Singapore,

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:19.300
which doesn't generally allow for dual citizenship.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:24.840
The actor reportedly spent around $15 million
on a swanky three-floor property and moved

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:29.760
his family to the tax-friendly island, following
in the footsteps of Facebook co-founder Eduardo

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.480
Saverin and fellow martial arts movie legend
Jackie Chan.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:38.280
The fact that he likely pays half of the amount
of tax he would be paying in the States was

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:43.330
surely a factor in Li's move, but according
to Nomad Capitalist, Singapore's excellent

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:46.360
education system also influenced Li's decision.

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:49.080
But how did the people of China take the news?

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:53.760
Traditionally, Chinese celebrities that ditch
the homeland for Singapore are dubbed traitors

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.940
and take a major hit to their reputation,
but strangely enough this didn't happen with

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:58.700
Li.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:03.340
According to the South China Morning Post,
polls revealed that only half of the Chinese

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:08.110
citizens asked about Li leaving China objected
to it, with one fan even suggesting that they

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.560
would like to do the same.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.620
That blogger wrote:

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.880
"It's [his] right to live where [he] wants
to.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.860
If I could, I will follow suit.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.280
[Singapore's] passport is better."

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:23.560
Rumors that Li was in grave health spread
like wildfire in 2018 after a photo of the

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:28.460
actor looking old and seemingly frail went
viral, forcing his manager to respond.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:33.800
Steven Chasman told USA Today that the story
was a lot of worrying over nothing, and Li

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.540
was simply in a bad light when he posed for
a quick snap with a fan.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:38.620
Chasman said:

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:42.140
"It's one picture and people are making these
interpretations from it.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:46.440
If you took a picture [of] me at the wrong
angle and wrong time of the day, I could look

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.510
frail as well."

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:51.980
Fans were quick to blame Li's grave new look
on his hyperthyroidism, which he had been

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:53.640
diagnosed with in 2010.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:58.419
While Li has been able to keep the condition
under control using medication, his health

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:01.600
has often become a cause for concern among
fans.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.580
In 2016, Li said:

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:07.720
"The web has been abuzz with news that I'm
going to be wheelchair-bound.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.620
Even my friends are concerned and are asking
how I am."

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:15.200
The action star has also joked that a wheelchair
company had been spreading the rumors to boost

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.140
sales.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:22.800
"And there was one medical appliance company
who came to me and asked me to endorse their

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:23.800
wheelchair."

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:27.360
He went on to reassure fans that he was a-okay,
saying:

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.699
"There is nothing to worry about my health."

00:08:29.699 --> 00:08:35.090
Li looked capable as ever in behind-the-scenes
footage from a 2017 short film, and Disney

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:39.830
is clearly confident in the actor's health,
as the Mouse House has cast him in its upcoming

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.660
live-action remake of Mulan.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:48.400
The devastation caused by the 2004 Boxing
Day tsunami can't easily be understated.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:55.020
On December 26th, a 9.2 magnitude earthquake
shook the seabed off the coast of Sumatra,

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:58.440
Indonesia, sending 40-foot waves hurtling
towards land.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:05.080
In the end, a staggering 230,000 people lost
their lives across 14 different countries,

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.820
one of which was the Maldives.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:12.570
Li and his family were vacationing on one
of the 26 ring-shaped atolls that make up

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:17.570
the South Asian republic when the tsunami
struck, and they had a very close and very

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:18.720
lucky escape.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.380
During a Hong Kong fundraiser, Li recalled:

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.180
"The waves came really quickly and formed
swirls.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:27.200
I carried my daughters and pulled my maid
and ran.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:31.840
I'd only walked three steps when I realized
that the water had already come up to my waist."

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:36.120
In a matter of seconds, the idyllic setting
had turned into something out of a nightmare.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.220
Li continued:

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.420
"When I looked back, everything I saw minutes
ago was gone.

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.300
Everything was surrounded by the ocean.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.680
The houses collapsed.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.960
I continued to run but the water was already
up to my mouth."

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:52.940
Luckily, Li, his family and his maid all survived
to tell the tale, which is apparently exactly

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.900
what the actor intends to do.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:10:00.300
In 2017, reports suggested that he was planning
to star in a film about the tsunami, as part

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.700
of a Chinese-Indonesian co-production.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.880
Surviving the tsunami changed Li's outlook
on life.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:11.780
The actor had an epiphany following the disaster,
deciding that he wanted to dedicate himself

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:16.450
to philanthropy after being deeply moved by
the treatment he and his family received from

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.760
total strangers.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.780
If it weren't for the actions of four brave
men who swam to Li's aid after he screamed

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:25.300
for help, his two youngest daughters would
have likely drowned.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:26.540
He later explained:

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:30.690
"The experience of surviving the chaos and
witnessing the devastation caused by this

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:33.360
natural disaster has changed me forever.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.800
During the recovery period in the Maldives,
I was deeply moved to see that everyone who

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:40.100
was able to help willingly pitched in.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:44.660
Never once did anyone ask, 'Where are you
from?' or 'What nationality are you?'

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:49.300
I wondered: was it possible to keep that spirit
alive and transcend traditional boundaries

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.360
to help humanity at large?"

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.080
The whole ordeal put life into perspective
for him.

00:10:54.089 --> 00:10:58.890
"I had spent the first 41 years of my life
thinking about Jet Li first, wanting to prove

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.460
I was special, wanting to prove I was a star."

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:04.080
So Li set up his own charitable foundation.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:04.720
He said:

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.460
"I realized that all the money and power in
the world would not have saved me from the

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.300
water.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:13.980
That night I decided I couldn't wait until
I was retired; I had to do something right

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:15.100
away."

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.200
